**`package.json`**
```json
{
  "name": "time-server",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Express server that returns the current time",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^4.19.2"
  }
}
```

**`server.js`**
```js
const express = require('express');

const app = express();
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

app.get('/time', (req, res) => {
  const now = new Date();
  res.json({
    iso: now.toISOString(),
    unix: Math.floor(now.getTime() / 1000),
    local: now.toString(),
  });
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server listening on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

To run it:
```bash
npm install
npm start
curl http://localhost:3000/time
```

`GET /time` returns JSON with the time in ISO 8601, Unix seconds and the server's local format. If you enable file writing, I can create the files and test the server.

